                <h2>1. Pre-Allocation Preparation Checklist</h2>
<p>Before planning your monthly ad budget, complete these items to ensure data-driven allocation decisions:</p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] <strong>Define core objectives for this period</strong>: Awareness/loyalty, product promotion, or cart abandonment recovery? Different goals mean different channel and budget priorities</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Review historical performance</strong>: What were CAC, ROAS, and conversion rates across channels last month? Which outperformed industry benchmarks?</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Assess product profit margins</strong>: Products with margins below 30% are not recommended for brand search campaigns</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Evaluate cash flow cycles</strong>: Sites with longer payment terms should reserve 15-20% as an emergency buffer</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Check account balance alerts</strong>: Ensure top-up cycles match ad spending pace to avoid interruptions from depleted balances</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Tip</strong>: For teams launching their first store, run a 7-day channel test with $300-500 before scaling.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>2. Budget Allocation Step-by-Step</h2>
<h3>Step 1: Divide Budget by Marketing Funnel Stage</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Funnel Stage</th>
<th>Recommended %</th>
<th>Core Purpose</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Awareness (reach, acquisition)</td>
<td>40-50%</td>
<td>Expand traffic pool</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Consideration (retargeting, bestsellers)</td>
<td>30-35%</td>
<td>Improve conversion rate</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Conversion (promotions, cart recovery)</td>
<td>15-20%</td>
<td>Increase AOV and repeat purchases</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Step 2: Allocate Test Budget vs. Scale Budget by Channel</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Test budget</strong>: Allocate 10-15% of daily budget to each new campaign, observe for 3-5 consecutive days</li>
<li><strong>Scale budget</strong>: Gradually increase spend on campaigns where CPA falls 20%+ below target</li>
<li><strong>Stop-loss mechanism</strong>: Pause campaigns with CPM 1.5x above category average or CTR below 1% within 72 hours</li>
</ul>
<h3>Step 3: Execute Channel-Specific Configuration</h3>
<p><strong>Meta (Facebook/Instagram)</strong>: Suitable for 50-60% of acquisition budget, focusing on image and video creative testing; can increase to 70% during product launch periods</p>
<p><strong>Google Ads</strong>: Search ads target category and brand terms; Shopping ads focus on top 20% SKUs by conversion rate; Display ads for retargeting</p>
<p><strong>TikTok</strong>: Recommend 15-20% during early testing phase, UGC-style short videos as primary format, keep conversion path short</p>
<p><strong>Email/Retargeting Tools</strong>: Cart abandonment rate typically 60-75%; reserve 5-10% budget specifically for recovery sequences</p>
<hr />
<h2>3. Post-Allocation Dynamic Checklist</h2>
<p>Conduct weekly budget health checks:</p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] <strong>Sufficient account balance?</strong> Top up when balance drops below 3x daily budget</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>ROAS targets met by channel?</strong> Channels below 1:3 require root cause analysis (creative vs. audience)</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Any campaigns over budget?</strong> Immediate review if daily spend exceeds budget by 150%</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>New vs. existing creative performance:</strong> New creatives should maintain 20-30% share to avoid creative fatigue</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Weekday vs. weekend spending variance:</strong> Adjust dayparting if variance exceeds 30%</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>4. Quick FAQ on Budget Allocation</h2>
<p><strong>Q: How to avoid uneven budget distribution with multiple accounts?</strong></p>
<p>Manage with "main account + test account" separation: main account takes 80% for stable scaling, test account uses 20% to explore new channels or product lines, with separate ROAS tracking for finance reconciliation.</p>
<p><strong>Q: How to adjust budget during peak seasons (promotions)?</strong></p>
<p>Start ramping up 2 weeks before promotions, focusing on retargeting during pre-launch; concentrate resources on conversion layer on promotion day, reducing awareness budget to 20%; maintain 15-20% recovery budget for 3 days post-promotion to capture remaining orders.</p>
<p><strong>Q: What to do if budget fluctuations trigger account restrictions?</strong></p>
<p>Avoid reducing daily budget by more than 50% at once; maintain 3-5 days of steady spending; if adjustments needed, limit daily changes to within 20%.</p>
